for the record Charles Miller uh 29F This body is reviewing a contract to secure $598,634 for the office of use of youth alternatives While the funding appears beneficial on the surface a structural audit of the contract timeline and data protocols reveals serious administrative compliance gaps First look at the exe execution timeline The performance period of this agreement explicitly states that work commenced on July 1st 2026 Yet the city attorney did not sign off on the form until September 21st 2026 and it is sitting before this committee today on October 6th This means municipal employees have been administering substance abuse testing and case management for over 90 days without a legally executed binding framework This is a severe breach of standard operating sequence that exposes the city to uncolateralized operational liabilities Second section 3 contains a structural imbalance regarding funding availability It grants the joint powers board the unilateral right

to terminate this agreement if state or county funding shifts providing only a 30-day notice with zero financial penalty or liquidation protections for the city The Office of Youth Alternatives have has already locked in fixed salary and fringe allocations based on this money including $222,859 for a diversion coordinator and $199,422 for a caseworker If the board pulls the plug the city's general fund is fully exposed these personal costs Third section 5 paragraph 1 establishes an aggressive data mandate City staff are legally required to upload highly sensitive tracking metrics into the reroute database posted by the University of Wyoming within two business days of any case update We are contractually locking our local department into strict rapid turnarounds for data tracking Yet there is zero reciprocal language protecting the data sovereignty or privacy rights of Cheyenne families from university level data handling liabilities I urge this committee to require a formal reconciliation of these retroactive operational dates before advancing the item Thank

